REMORA biology extension implementation plan
Version 2: abstract ecosystem interface and optional module composition
23 October 2026

Provide one abstract Biology interface with concrete ecosystem implementations
such as FennelBiology, ECBBiology, and NemuroBiology. Provide a separate optional
module interface so a user can add processes to a selected ecosystem without
copying its kernel or adding model-specific branches throughout REMORA.

Retain REMORA's existing scalar storage, transport, forcing, and biology call
site. Preserve the reference ecosystem's numerical equations exactly during
the initial port and architecture refactor. In particular, add no clipping,
floors, ceilings, or denominator guards, including on intermediate quantities,
unless they are already part of the selected reference implementation.

This revision specifies the capability to attach additional biology modules.
It does not propose implementing an oyster model or another new scientific
module. An oyster extension mentioned by the user is an illustrative use case
for the interface, field mapping, and optional persistent-state lifecycle.

This is a documentation-only implementation proposal. No REMORA or ROMS source
code is changed by this document. The original plan is retained separately.

